    {
      "id": "wjmveyi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Mineral Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Minerals are naturally occurring inorganic substances possessing a definite chemical composition and structural arrangement.",
        "India's primary mineral wealth is concentrated across distinct belts, notably the North-Eastern Peninsular, South-Western, and North-Western belts.",
        "Metallic minerals such as iron ore, bauxite, and manganese provide the structural foundation for India's heavy manufacturing and metallurgical industries.",
        "Coal remains the primary source of commercial energy in India, supplemented by domestic petroleum extraction and non-conventional energy sources.",
        "Because mineral deposits are non-renewable and finite, strategic conservation and sustainable resource management are essential."
      ],
      "id": "gct5isi"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ovcetq",
      "content": "• Minerals are natural substances found in rocks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ozh120t",
      "content": "• They are formed through geological processes over millions of years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rpx66mz",
      "content": "• Minerals are essential raw materials for industries."
    },
